  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "div_function",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_operators.c",
    "description": "In the slow scalar-conversion path for in-place division (`result == op1`), `div_function()` destroys the original left-hand zval at line 1391 before retrying with converted operands. If that retry returns `DIV_BY_ZERO`, control reaches `div_by_zero`, but the function only marks the result undefined when `result != op1`. Thus the in-place result remains a refcounted zval pointing to already-freed storage. The `ZEND_ASSIGN_OP` handler then treats the compound-assignment result as valid and, when the expression result is used, `ZVAL_COPY()` attempts to addref the dangling allocation, causing the UAF in `zend_gc_addref`.",
    "conditions": "Trigger an in-place compound division (`/=`) whose left operand requires scalar-to-number conversion and owns refcounted storage (notably a numeric string), while the converted right operand is zero, and use the value of the compound-assignment expression so `RETURN_VALUE_USED` is true. In the PoV, the fuzzed PHP reaches `$$h /= $i - 20.0` when the denominator becomes zero; the converted left string is destroyed, the division-by-zero retry leaves its stale zval in place, and the assignment-op result copy addrefs that freed string."
  },
